<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The com.apple.security.application-groups key is removed on purpose.
    A free Apple team grants no App Group. A sideload profile from AltStore or
    SideStore lacks the key. So an .ipa that requests it fails to install.

    ponytail: this removal parks three features. They are:
      1. the iOS share sheet (the DaakShareExtension.appex is not embedded);
      2. the Siri and Shortcuts send (DaakIntentBridge);
      3. the notification-action stash (DaakNotifyActionStash).
    The three Swift call sites fail soft on a nil container. The app still runs.

    To re-enable the three features:
      1. restore this key in Daak.entitlements;
      2. restore this key in DaakShareExtension.entitlements;
      3. restore the DaakShareExtension.appex entry in the
         "Embed App Extensions" build phase of Daak.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj;
      4. pay for the Apple Developer Program, which grants the App Group.
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
